<h2 id="data-processing">Schedule: Data Processing Terms (UK GDPR Article 28)</h2>
<p>1. <strong>Roles.</strong> For personal data about your pupils, their parents, and your instructors and staff that is put into DriveSchoolPro, you are the controller and we are your processor.</p>
<p>2. <strong>Details of the processing.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>Subject matter and duration:</em> providing the Service for as long as your account is open, plus the periods in clause 7.3.</li>
<li><em>Nature and purpose:</em> scheduling, pupil records and progress tracking, messaging, payments, document storage and AI lesson briefings.</li>
<li><em>Types of data:</em> names, contact details and dates of birth; lesson, progress and payment records; notes you add; driving licence and ID documents you upload; and <strong>special category data</strong>: health information in medical notes and medical certificates, where you choose to record it.</li>
<li><em>Data subjects:</em> pupils (including some aged 16 to 17), parents, instructors and staff.</li>
</ul>
<p>3. <strong>Instructions.</strong> We process the data only to provide the Service, on your documented instructions (these Terms and your use of the Service), unless the law requires otherwise. If it does, we'll tell you first unless the law forbids that.</p>
<p>4. <strong>Confidentiality.</strong> Everyone who handles the data for us is bound by confidentiality.</p>
<p>5. <strong>Security.</strong> We take appropriate technical and organisational measures, including encryption in transit and at rest, role-based access, logging and backups.</p>
<p>6. <strong>Sub-processors.</strong> You authorise the sub-processors listed on our <a href="/subprocessors/">sub-processors page</a>. We'll give at least 30 days' notice of any new one by email. If you object, you may cancel before the change and receive a refund of prepaid fees for the period after it. Each sub-processor is bound by data protection terms that give at least the same protection, and we remain responsible for them. Health data in medical notes is not sent to our AI provider.</p>
<p>7. <strong>International transfers.</strong> Where personal data is transferred outside the UK, we use a lawful mechanism: UK adequacy regulations, the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, or the UK International Data Transfer Addendum.</p>
<p>8. <strong>Assistance.</strong> We'll help you, as far as reasonably possible, with requests from people exercising their data rights (we'll pass on any request we receive), security, breach notification and data protection impact assessments.</p>
<p>9. <strong>Breaches.</strong> We'll tell you without undue delay, and in any case within 48 hours, after becoming aware of a personal data breach affecting your data.</p>
<p>10. <strong>End of the account.</strong> When your account closes, clause 7.3 of the Terms applies.</p>
<p>11. <strong>Audits.</strong> We'll make available the information you reasonably need to show compliance, and allow a reasonable audit not more than once a year, on 30 days' notice, at your cost.</p>
<p>12. <strong>Your obligations.</strong> You confirm that you have a lawful basis for the personal data you put into the Service, that you have an Article 9 condition for any health data, and that you have told pupils how their data is used.</p>

